 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed changes are pushed to browsers over self-hosted WebSockets, requiring replayable revisions and reliable publication in the change store, session management in delivery, and reconnect/catch-up logic in browsers. Five-second HTTPS polling and a hosted realtime service were rejected to get fast updates without vendor lock-in, accepting responsibility for connection capacity and reconnect operations. See [the change delivery decision](decisions/change-delivery-approach.md).
